{"sequence":55,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T14:57:18.482795524Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-4-7dfb6287","body":"The `check_strictly_increasing` helper in crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:398-409 only reports the upper field name and value in its error. When the invariant fires (e.g., `optimal_temp_min_c >= optimal_temp_max_c`), the error says `InvariantViolation { field: \"shrimp_params.optimal_temp_max_c\", value: X }` without mentioning the lower bound that caused the conflict. Consider including both field names or a more descriptive message to aid debugging.","dedup_key":"dba0b581a2faabe1574bf24b6f08af829e454225706d59ed4fb6bff867681c2a","run_id":"run-20260328132625","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
