{"sequence":68,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T15:28:48.089069200Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-5-98d4fd2c","body":"In `compute_co2_kla` (chemistry.rs:55-58), the Euler stability cap is baked into the function (`k_la_o2.min(1.0) * 0.91`), while the O2 path caps K_LA at the *usage site* (dissolved_oxygen.rs:94). This asymmetry means `compute_co2_kla` always returns a stability-capped value, making it unsuitable if a caller ever needs the true physical CO2 K_LA (e.g., for diagnostic display or reporting). Consider either: (a) renaming `compute_co2_kla` to `compute_co2_kla_capped` to signal the cap is embedded, or (b) refactoring both O2 and CO2 paths to cap at the same level (either always at definition or always at usage). This is not a correctness bug today since the only caller is the Euler step, but it's a maintainability trap for the next contributor.","dedup_key":"d1198166d8a7f35c3bb3a94f4fb3447ac3f120e99ba893755ffc956310cb83ca","run_id":"run-20260328132625","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":69,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T15:28:48.097971037Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-5-24b63d9b","body":"Reset `spawn_progress_accum` when the adult population or eligible spawner count drops to zero. The new accumulator is persisted in `crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs:128-131`, and `spawning()` both consumes it at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:443-444` and returns early at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:425-435` without clearing it. That means a later, unrelated colony can inherit fractional spawn progress from a deleted one. I reproduced this by stepping a 10-adult colony at `base_spawn_rate=0.35`, then resetting to a clean 2-adult colony: with the reused carry the new colony produced 1 berried female on day 1, while a clean 2-adult colony produced 0. Clear the accumulator whenever spawning continuity is broken.","dedup_key":"9ce8186a4c6c928f9f1c28bb1d01c883759c53d37e38f66546813949b40f436c","run_id":"run-20260328132625","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":70,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T15:28:48.106967422Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-5-a50e6e2d","body":"Reset `hatch_success_carry` whenever all berried females / egg cohorts are cleared. The accumulator is also persisted in `crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs:128-131`, but `egg_development()` reuses it at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:517-520` and can return with no cohorts at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:465-475` without zeroing it; `clamp_berried_to_adults()` at `crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs:546-553` can also delete cohorts without touching the carry. That lets a brand-new clutch inherit old fractional hatch credit. I reproduced this with `hatch_success_base=0.3`: after one large cohort left a positive carry, a later single-cohort state hatched 2 juveniles immediately, while the same clean single-cohort state hatched 0. Clear the carry whenever the hatch process loses continuity.","dedup_key":"98173c06640337c635d656bf0e104a168d76cdc458780318601274cee637a6da","run_id":"run-20260328132625","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
